Step 1 — Create the project
Open UiPath Studio
Click New → Process
Name it:
MovieRatingBot
Click Create
Step 2 — Create Input Dialog
In Activities, search:
Input Dialog
Drag it into Main Sequence.

Set:

Title

Movie Rating

Label

Enter movie name:
Create output variable

Find Output → Result.

Click the variable field and create:

movieName

Type:

String

So:

Input Dialog
Result → movieName
Step 3 — Open IMDb search

Below Input Dialog:

Add Use Application/Browser.
Click Indicate Application.
Open Chrome.
For the URL, use:
"https://www.imdb.com/find/?q=" + movieName

⚠️ Keep the quotation marks around the URL part.

Example

If user enters:

Avatar

UiPath opens:

https://www.imdb.com/find/?q=Avatar
Step 4 — Click the movie

Inside Use Application/Browser → Do:

Add Click.
Click Indicate on screen.
On IMDb search results, select the movie title you want.
Usually select the first matching movie.

Example:

Avatar
2009

Click that movie.

Your workflow becomes:

Input Dialog
     ↓
Use Application/Browser
     ↓
Click Movie
Step 5 — Get the rating

After the Click activity:

Add Get Text.
Click Indicate on screen.
IMDb movie page will be shown.
Select the rating number.

For example:

7.8
Create output variable

In Get Text → Text value (Out):

Create:

movieRating

Type:

String

So:

Get Text
Text value → movieRating
Step 6 — Display the result

Below Get Text:

Add Message Box.
In the message field enter:
"Movie: " + movieName + vbCrLf + "IMDb Rating: " + movieRating
